<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11716" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crūdesco</span></b> , dŭi,
		3, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch.
				n.</i> [crudus], <i>to grow harsh</i> or <i>violent, to increase, grow worse</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">perh. not before Virg.): coepit crudescere
					morbus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 3, 504</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pugnae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					7, 788</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ferrum magicā linguā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					1, 431</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 680</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crudescente irā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					8, 4, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seditio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. H.
					3, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">noxa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 8, 57</span></i>
			.</div>
